              "content": "The two series are different TREATMENTS, not control and test.\n\n`routed_full_window:0` \u2014 sample-only reassignment. Only the online gate moved these projects, and only for sessions analyzed since the last pass, so coverage RAMPS down across the trailing 7-day window as it turns over.\n\n**Expect this arm to move barely at all on small projects, and do NOT read that as the gate behaving well.** The build path re-assigns every sampled member with no fit floor, and 41 of 45 measured projects have a whole 7-day window that fits inside the 1,500 sample cap \u2014 so gardening overwrites the online decision every ~6h. On those projects the floor governs only the hours between a session being analyzed and the next pass.\n\n`routed_full_window:1` \u2014 full-window routing (adaptive). The online gate AND the reassignment floor moved these, and the whole window is re-gated every pass, so coverage STEPS on the first pass. This is the only arm where the floor is not overwritten.\n\nIt is the plan's shape, not its mode: an enforced run that fell back to static takes the sample-only path. Do not read a gap between the arms as an effect of the clustering mode.\n\nOnly whole-project topic runs emit this span \u2014 a view's assignments live in a different table, so a cohort or facet run would report the project's numbers under its own id.\n\nExact pre-change numbers are not here \u2014 the observation rows behind them expire on the 30-day retention horizon. They live in the committed ClickHouse baseline (`apps/workflows/datadog/taxonomy-assignment-baseline.json`), whose `wouldRejectAtFloor` column is the per-project prediction to check `assigned_share` against.",
